<form class="fso-obs-helper">
  <p>Add a <strong>Browser Source</strong> in OBS and use the URL below. The page is transparent and designed to sit over your game/video layout.</p>

  <div class="form-group">
    <label for="fso-obs-url">OBS Browser Source URL</label>
    <div class="form-fields">
      <input id="fso-obs-url" type="text" value="{{obsUrl}}" readonly>
      <button type="button" data-action="copy-url"><i class="fas fa-copy"></i> Copy OBS URL</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="form-group">
    <label>Recommended Size</label>
    <div class="form-fields">
      <input type="text" value="{{width}} × {{height}}" readonly>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="notes"><strong>OBS:</strong> Sources → + → Browser → paste this URL → set Width 1920 and Height 1080.</p>
  <p class="notes"><strong>First OBS login:</strong> Right-click the Browser Source → <strong>Interact</strong> → select your dedicated Stream/Spectator Foundry user → enter its password if required → Join Game. OBS keeps its own browser session, separate from Chrome.</p>
  <p class="notes"><strong>Test Overlay</strong> opens the URL in a normal browser tab so you can verify the overlay separately from OBS.</p>

  <div class="form-group">
    <button type="button" data-action="test-overlay"><i class="fas fa-external-link-alt"></i> Open Test in Browser</button>
  </div>
</form>
